From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: npu: pre-check DONE across multi-descriptor RX frames

mt76_npu_dequeue() walks up to NPU_RX_DMA_PKT_COUNT_MASK descriptors of one
NPU RX frame.  When a descriptor's NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE bit is still clear,
bailing out mid-loop after building the head skb either double-frees
descriptor 0's page_pool buffer on rollback (when q->tail is not advanced)
or hands a truncated skb up the stack while leaving the trailing fragments
orphaned at q->tail (when breaking out and advancing q->tail).

Pre-check NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK across all descriptors 0..nframes-1
before consuming any descriptor or page_pool buffer.  If any descriptor in
the multi-descriptor frame is not ready yet, return NULL with q->tail,
q->queued and every buffer untouched so the next poll completes the whole
frame cleanly.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
---
--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -67,19 +67,38 @@ static struct sk_buff *mt76_npu_dequeue(
 	int i, nframes, index = q->tail;
 	struct sk_buff *skb = NULL;
 
+	if (!q->queued ||
+	    !FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK, desc[index].ctrl))
+		return NULL;
+
+	dma_rmb();
+
 	nframes = FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_PKT_COUNT_MASK, desc[index].info);
 	nframes = max_t(int, nframes, 1);
 
+	if (nframes > q->queued)
+		return NULL;
+
+	/*
+	 * Verify every descriptor of a multi-descriptor frame is DONE before
+	 * consuming any page_pool buffer or advancing q->tail.  Bailing out
+	 * mid-loop either double-frees descriptor 0 on rollback or delivers
+	 * a truncated frame and leaves the trailing fragments orphaned.
+	 */
+	for (i = 1; i < nframes; i++) {
+		int idx = (index + i) % q->ndesc;
+
+		if (!FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK, desc[idx].ctrl))
+			return NULL;
+	}
+	if (nframes > 1)
+		dma_rmb();
+
 	for (i = 0; i < nframes; i++) {
 		struct mt76_queue_entry *e = &q->entry[index];
 		int len = FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_CUR_LEN_MASK,
 				    desc[index].ctrl);
 
-		if (!FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK, desc[index].ctrl)) {
-			dev_kfree_skb(skb);
-			return NULL;
-		}
-
 		dma_sync_single_for_cpu(dev->dma_dev, e->dma_addr[0],
 					e->dma_len[0],
 					page_pool_get_dma_dir(q->page_pool));
